  "source": {
    "title": "Portadown Express, 23 January 1920, p. 5 (\"Majority of old members returned at Tandragee\"); withdrawals from the Lurgan Mail, 17 January 1920, p. 5",
    "publisher": "Portadown Express (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every name read from the page image; the report gives no vote figures"
  },
  "note": "Proportional representation, one area for the whole town. Twenty candidates were nominated and four withdrew (T. Aston, George Crothers, T. Thompson and J. Stone), leaving sixteen for nine seats. White, Coburn, Meredith, Neill and Roberts were old members, as was the defeated William Davison. The report prints the elected and defeated but no first preferences or counts; 13 spoilt papers. Edward Maginnis (Labour) elected and C. Maginnis defeated, as the Portadown Express (23 Jan 1920, p. 5), Lurgan Mail, Northern Whig and Irish Weekly (all 24 Jan 1920) print it; the Irish Independent's \"C. M'Guinness (U.)\" (19 and 24 Jan 1920) is its own error."
}
